WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.930
A 1993 DOS

00:00:01.742 --> 00:00:02.201
game

00:00:02.437 --> 00:00:03.239
rebuilt for a

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.595
RISC-V FPGA

00:00:05.118 --> 00:00:06.580
Bertrand Fan released

00:00:06.451 --> 00:00:08.007
an openFPGA core

00:00:07.818 --> 00:00:08.596
that plays the

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.577
1993 game SkyRoads

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:11.214
on the Analogue

00:00:11.026 --> 00:00:11.686
Pocket

00:00:12.214 --> 00:00:13.063
It isn't an

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:13.747
emulator

00:00:13.886 --> 00:00:15.406
The FPGA hosts

00:00:15.242 --> 00:00:16.338
a small RISC-V

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.105
system running the

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.461
game's decompiled C

00:00:18.273 --> 00:00:18.862
code

00:00:19.004 --> 00:00:19.994
The listing says

00:00:19.806 --> 00:00:20.572
the game is

00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:21.161
freeware

00:00:21.686 --> 00:00:24.032
Version 0.2.2 fixes

00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:24.952
music voices that

00:00:24.764 --> 00:00:25.895
went missing because

00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:26.851
sound-chip register

00:00:26.662 --> 00:00:27.853
writes were spaced

00:00:27.665 --> 00:00:28.820
too closely at

00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:30.011
the Pocket's 49

00:00:29.823 --> 00:00:30.954
megahertz clock

00:00:31.494 --> 00:00:32.508
Full story on

00:00:32.319 --> 00:00:33.215
the dashboard
